NetHack is somewhat unbalanced, i mean, everyone uses long swords or
daggers, gets mithril, goes to the castle, and gets some dsm flavor,
then wins.
Tell me what you think about this:
These are my ideas to balance some weapons, armour and monsters, will
post the remaining later.
-Merge dagger, knife, short sword and saber skills into Short Blades
-Merge broadsword, long sword and scimitar into Long Blades
-Merge spear, trident, and polearms into Polearms, make them useful in
melee without the need to ride
-Merge mace, club, hammer and morningstar into Maces
-Merge dart, shuriken, boomerang and javelin into Throwables
-Merge whip and flail into Flails
-Merge axes and battleaxes into Axes
-Increase the rarity of long swords a lot, not being dropped by any
kind of soldier
-Remove the long sword from valkyries' starting equipment, give them a
scimitar instead
-Buff armor: leather (3 ac, 50 weight, mc1), studded leather (4 ac, 60
weight, mc1), chain mail (5ac, 70 weight, mc1) ,remove ring mail,
scale mail (6 ac, 80 weight, mc2), remove orcish ring and chain mails,
remove banded mail, remove mithril, splint mail (8 ac, 130 weight,
mc2), plate mail (10 ac, 200 weight, mc3), bronze plate mail (13 ac,
250 weight, mc3), and crystal plate mail (15 ac, 300 weight,
reflection, mc3), make the plate mails rare (the yendorian army can't
be generated with them, they get scale instead of plate and splint
instead of crystal plate)
-Unique captain @ guarding the castle, guaranteed crystal plate mail,
gloves, helm and boots, 50% chance of a large shield and a katana,
otherwise a two-handed sword. Base speed 12 (Yes, as fast as you are
in that heavy armor), base damage 6d4, 6d4, base ac 10, HD 15, HP 110,
MR 90, alignment -15, difficulty 22, human properties. You know, to
make the castle a bit more exciting
-Nerf DSM: (200 weight, 8 ac)
-Knights get +0 studded leather instead of +1 ring mail
-Samurai get scale mail instead of splint mail
-Make a new skill, equivalent to "two weapon combat", "two-handed
weapons" that improves the accuracy with a twohander
-Make twohanders have somewhat painful (-7 or so) to-hit penalties
-Be unable to get both cold resistance and fire resistance
intrinsically
-Change base damage of halberd (3d7), bardiche (d17), spetum(d10),
bill-guisarme(2d7), voulge(2d6), ranseur(d8), glaive(d15),
partisan(d6), remove all other polearms
-Remove damage versus small, and make the damage versus large the base
damage for all weapons
-Change base damage of two-handed sword(2d8 + d6), battleaxe(3d6) and
tsurugi(3d8)
-Remove the twohander from barbarians' starting equipment
-Give the tsurugi of muramasa an #invoke that performs blessed remove
curse, remove its instakill, change its bonus damage to 2d8
-Give the heart of ahriman displacement and invocable flight
-Wands of speed monster have the same effect as the haste self spell
-Remove amnesia
-Make flayers ignore E a la minotaur (stat death is still a threat,
making rings of sustain abilities far more valuable)
-Make all & ignore E
-Remove Demogorgon's instakill, make him hit a lot harder, kind of
like Kaen
-Remove 100% damage reduction from a resistance, make it 85% (No more
godly chars, things can hurt you now!)
-Change the base damage of long swords(d9), axes(d8), hammers(d7),
sabers (d9),
-Double the speed and hp of all non-unique &
-Add "Spiked flails", one-handed, d10 damage, flails skill
-Summoned monsters give no xp, don't drop corpses, drop no items, and
aren't permanent.
-Remove the "teleport to the stairs" thing by covetous monsters. They
can and will teleport to you if you teleport away, though.
-Make Geryon speed 12 and Juiblex speed 6 and digging-inmune
-Substitute the valley's priest with Geryon. He is generated
meditating, so no teleport to you, even if a lich aggravates monsters
-Give the orb of detection invocable magic mapping (Seems fitting, at
least more than invocable invisibility)


